name: Branch Boundary Guard (PRs → __PROD_BRANCH__)

# =============================================================================
# LOOM-SCAFFOLD-MARKER: environment-promotion
#
# Generated by /scaffold-environments for THIS repository's topology, from
# .docs/policies/environment-promotion-policy.md § 3 ("the branch boundary
# belongs in CI, not in convention"). Generalized from LogicLoom's own
# branch-topology-guard.yml, which is the reference implementation — the regex
# below is YOURS, composed from the branches this repository actually had when
# the scaffolder ran:
#
#     production  : __PROD_BRANCH__
#     integration : __INTEGRATION_BRANCH_DISPLAY__
#     staging     : __STAGING_BRANCH_DISPLAY__
#
# WHAT IT DOES: hard-fails any pull request whose BASE is '__PROD_BRANCH__'
# unless its HEAD is one of the branches allowed to reach production. A stated
# branching convention is not a boundary; this is.
#
# THREE PROPERTIES WORTH KEEPING WHEN YOU EDIT IT:
#
#   1. IT FAILS CLOSED. An empty `github.head_ref` is a FAILURE, not a pass, and
#      it prints why (§ 4.2 — fail closed with a typed reason). A gate that
#      cannot evaluate its own condition must never pass optimistically.
#   2. IT HAS NO EXEMPTIONS. No label, no actor allowlist, no skip flag. Every
#      escape hatch is a route for exactly the content the gate exists to stop.
#      Widening ALLOWED_HEAD_REGEX is a reviewable change to this file; a skip
#      label is not.
#   3. IT IS TAMPER-PROOF BY PLACEMENT. For `pull_request` events GitHub
#      evaluates the workflow from the BASE branch, so a PR cannot modify the
#      copy of this file that judges it. That property only holds while this
#      file exists ON '__PROD_BRANCH__'. Merge it there.
#
# THIS IS NOT DEPLOY MACHINERY. It runs no deployment, no migration, and no
# seed. It reads one branch name and decides. LogicLoom ships no pipeline —
# see environment-promotion-policy.md § 10.
#
# TO WIDEN IT (e.g. a hotfix line that legitimately reaches production
# directly), edit the ONE line marked below — for example:
#     '^(__ALLOWED_HEAD_ALTERNATIVES__|hotfix/.+)$'
# and understand that you are widening the boundary, not adding an exemption.
#
# TO DELETE IT: if '__PROD_BRANCH__' legitimately takes feature branches
# directly, this gate is wrong for you. Delete the file. That is a supported
# answer, not a failure.
# =============================================================================

on:
  pull_request:
    branches: [__PROD_BRANCH__]
    types: [opened, reopened, synchronize]

permissions:
  contents: read

jobs:
  branch-boundary:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - name: Assert PR head may target __PROD_BRANCH__
        env:
          HEAD_REF: ${{ github.head_ref }}
          # ── THE ONE LINE TO EDIT ─────────────────────────────────────────
          ALLOWED_HEAD_REGEX: '^(__ALLOWED_HEAD_ALTERNATIVES__)$'
          PROD_BRANCH: '__PROD_BRANCH__'
        run: |
          set -euo pipefail
          if [ -z "${HEAD_REF:-}" ]; then
            echo "::error::Could not determine the PR head branch (github.head_ref is empty) — failing closed."
            echo "REASON: this gate cannot evaluate its own condition without a head ref, and a gate that cannot evaluate itself must fail, not pass. There is no override."
            exit 1
          fi
          if printf '%s' "$HEAD_REF" | grep -qE "$ALLOWED_HEAD_REGEX"; then
            echo "branch-boundary: head '$HEAD_REF' is permitted to target '$PROD_BRANCH'"
            exit 0
          fi
          echo "::error::PR head branch '$HEAD_REF' may not target '$PROD_BRANCH'."
          cat <<EOF
          ------------------------------------------------------------------
          CAUSE
            '$PROD_BRANCH' is this repository's production line. It accepts only
            a head branch matching:
                $ALLOWED_HEAD_REGEX
            '$HEAD_REF' does not match, so this PR would move code into
            production without passing through the promotion path.

          REMEDY
            Land your work on the integration branch first, then promote:
              1. Re-target this PR at __REMEDY_TARGET__ instead of '$PROD_BRANCH'.
              2. Promote through your declared chain
                 (.logic-loom/config/environments.conf).

          EXEMPTIONS
            None. There is deliberately no label, actor, or skip flag. If your
            topology genuinely needs another head branch to reach production,
            widen ALLOWED_HEAD_REGEX in
            .github/workflows/branch-boundary-guard.yml — a reviewable change —
            rather than adding an escape hatch.
          ------------------------------------------------------------------
          EOF
          exit 1
